
What is Data Structure
- It is the way by which we can store the data in efficient way.


Type of DataStructure:
   1. Primitive Data Structure(eg. Boolean,char,byte,short,int,long )
        - primitive used in develop simple application (eg. Calculator,SnakeGame,Currency Convater)
   2. Non-Primitive Data Structure
        - Non-Primitive used in (eg. e-Commerce,social Networking,Banking)
        -Because application run fast

        2. Non-Primitive Data Structure:
            1. Linear Data Structure (eg. String,Array,List,Set,Queue,ArrayList,LinkedList,HashSet,LinkHashset)
            2. Non-Linear Data Structure (eg. Graph,Trees)

